WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:06.420
Hello, and thank you again for joining us
for this NCBI minute.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:11.920
Today we will explore the save search feature
which can provide automatic email updates

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:18.590
on a daily weekly or monthly basis, and conclude
with creating a customized named collection

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:23.400
from our search results that can be made public
to share with others.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.550
Let's get started with saving and managing
a search.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:34.450
The easiest way to begin is at the PubMed
home page located at www.pubmed.gov.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:39.670
If you are not already signed into NCBI, don't
worry you will be prompted later.

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:46.609
For my example, I am automating my PubMed
search for Adolescent COPD.

00:00:46.609 --> 00:00:51.309
Step 1 is to enter my query or search terms.

00:00:51.309 --> 00:00:54.460
If you are interested in a tutorial on how
to construct a query,

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:57.629
information will be provided at the end of
this presentation.

00:00:57.629 --> 00:01:02.780
But in general, the PubMed process is from
left to right and

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:07.080
dates and ranges are not recommended for saved
searches.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:09.570
Step 2 Click the Search button.

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:14.400
Next, click 'create alert', which is located
beneath the search bar.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.940
A popup window will appear.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:23.070
Again, if you are not logged into your NCBI
account, you will be prompted to sign in.

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:25.630
Now it's time to save the search name.

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:27.820
The default is the search.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:29.560
A couple of things to remember.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:35.560
The saved search name may be up to 100 characters
long and this will become the subject line

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:37.940
of your email.

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:42.030
Queries can be quite cumbersome, so I updated
it.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:46.070
Next, is the original search query from PubMed.

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:50.000
You are also able to modify your terms from
here.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.370
If you edit your search terms, always remember
to click Test search terms.

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:59.820
This will provide the number of items based
on the edited search.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:05.320
Although I did not modify the search, it shows
that there are 3 thousand 1 hundred and 31

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:08.590
results found at the time of this screenshot.

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:12.280
Do you want your new search results sent automatically
to your email?

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:15.860
I do, so Yes, please is selected.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:20.480
We will discuss a little later what happens
if you say No, thanks.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:25.480
Next, visually confirm your email address,remembering
that

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:29.590
Automatic e-mail updates can only be sent
to e-mail address

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:31.650
that have been confirmed.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:37.480
If an e-mail bounces back three times, the
email address will be changed to unconfirmed.

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:44.310
Also, you may consider adding nih.gov to your
email safe list.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:47.709
If you do not know how to do this, please
contact your email

00:02:47.709 --> 00:02:51.569
provider's customer support for assistance.

00:02:51.569 --> 00:02:55.490
To verify that your email address is confirmed,
click on your username

00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:57.459
or Change.

00:02:57.459 --> 00:03:00.890
As you can see, the email address has been
confirmed.

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:06.270
Otherwise, a link would appear allowing you
to resend the confirmation email.

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:11.650
Now, let's return to saved searches and
schedule the frequency of the email.

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:16.990
For monthly, choices include:
-The first Sunday through Saturday.

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:22.260
-The first day of the month
- or The first WEEKDAY of the month.

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:26.459
- Weekly
- And finally, daily.

00:03:26.459 --> 00:03:28.940
Next, select the format.

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:33.760
The choices are Summary, Abstract and Medline.

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:36.490
Let's take a look at the actual email.

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:40.920
The examples shown are from Outlook 2016.

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:49.349
All emails consist of the name of the saved
search and in this one I re-edited the name.

00:03:49.349 --> 00:03:53.930
Sender's message is optional text that can
be included in each email.

00:03:53.930 --> 00:04:04.530
Next, is the date sent, my PubMed search terms,
the ability to view the complete results in

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:11.340
PubMed, the ability to edit the search, and
of course unsubscribe.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:16.840
And finally, the PubMed emailed results in
Summary format.

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:23.340
Here is an example of how the same result
as it appears in the Abstract format.

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:26.540
And in the Medline format.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:29.740
Back to our customized Saved Search.

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:33.500
Select the maximum number of items to appear
in the email.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:39.460
In order to verify that the alert is running
properly, use send even when there aren't

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:41.490
any new search results.

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:47.490
In the event an update is not sent out as
scheduled or incomplete, the next scheduled

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:50.640
update will include the missing items.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:56.530
Here, you may include any optional text that
you wish to be added to your email.

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:57.750
And click save.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:03.280
You will be immediately taken back to the
PubMed search page and will see the confirmation

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:04.720
here.

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:09.150
You are also able to edit your search settings
at any time if needed.

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:14.830
Earlier, I pointed out that you could click
'No, thanks' to an email search result.

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:20.160
Let's take a quick look at My NCBI where the
saved search is stored.

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:28.240
Since we are logged into NCBI, click the My
NCBI link located next to your username.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:33.150
As you can see, in the saved searches portlet,
there are two PubMed Searches.

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:39.180
The one we just created Adolescent COPD and
another Lung Cancer.

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:42.350
For Lung Cancer, I selected 'no, thanks'.

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:45.590
I do not want email updates.

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:51.500
The 'What's New' column shows that there are
220 citations currently available since I

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:54.440
last looked at my results 3 days ago.

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:57.600
'What's new' is available for all searches.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:02.060
For example, if Adolescent COPD delivers on
a weekly basis,

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:09.050
I can still log into NCBI to see if there
are added citations since my last email run

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:13.120
and view the citations by clicking on the
numbered link.

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:18.560
The 'Saved Search' portlet has the ability
to manage saved searches.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:23.570
From here, you can quickly look at your scheduled
email delivery and edit your saved search

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:27.690
by clicking either on the gear or schedule
link.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:34.020
If you check the box next to the search name,
you are able to Delete the selected item or

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:36.900
items and also see what's new.

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:43.880
Now, let's talk about building a collection
by going back to the My NCBI homepage.

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:50.770
My NCBI comes with default collections of
My Bibliography, Other Citations and Favorites.

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:56.940
Today, we will be creating a customizable
titled collection to share with others.

00:06:56.940 --> 00:07:02.240
For your convenience, we have great tutorials
on the default collections

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:05.970
that will be included at the end of this presentation.

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:11.050
Although we are starting from saved searches,
you may also conduct a search directly in

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:12.240
PubMed.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:17.090
Remember, clicking on Lung Cancer beneath
the PubMed Searches column

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:20.470
will re-run the search and display the results
in PubMed.

00:07:20.470 --> 00:07:27.550
Likewise, if I click the link under 'What's
New', I will only have access to the 220

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:30.780
new citations based on my search.

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:37.830
From here we are taken to PubMed, which contains
my saved search results.

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:43.430
Select a few of the citations for the collection
and click 'Send to'.

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:49.941
If all of the citations should be included
, simply click 'send to' and up to 1,000 citations

00:07:49.941 --> 00:07:52.940
will be added to the collection.

00:07:52.940 --> 00:08:00.020
Select the destination of 'Collections',
verify the number of items selected, and click

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:01.190
'Add to collections'.

00:08:01.190 --> 00:08:07.789
The pop out window will automatically show
'Append to an existing collection'.

00:08:07.789 --> 00:08:12.230
This is where the pre-defined collection 'favorites'
and personally titled

00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:13.730
collections will reside.

00:08:13.730 --> 00:08:16.430
Today we are creating a new collection.

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:21.710
So we will enter the name of the collection
and click save.

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:27.889
We are returned to the PubMed page where we
receive a confirmation of the saved items

00:08:27.889 --> 00:08:35.560
and the opportunity to edit the collection
lung cancer in My NCBI.

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:39.700
You are also able to return to the My NCBI
homepage by clicking on

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:44.490
the My NCBI link located next to your username.

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:47.330
Lung cancer now appears in the collection.

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:55.960
Today we will click 'edit' to make the collection
public and to generate a URL to share.

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:59.350
In the gold box, click the link 'make it public'.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:05.459
Confirmation of the update will appear above
the gold box, along with the generated URL

00:09:05.459 --> 00:09:08.290
for this collection.

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:14.410
URL retrieval is located in edit settings,
found in the gold tool bar,

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:19.830
By clicking on the gear next to the collection
from the My NCBI homepage

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:26.860
or the link Private/Public also located on
the My NCBI homepage.

00:09:26.860 --> 00:09:30.180
From the edit page
- You can modify the name of the collection

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:37.040
- Make the collection private or public
- Retrieve the URL for the public collection

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:40.390
- and gather the HTML code.

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:45.070
If the collection was public and changed back
to private, the URL and HTML will no longer

00:09:45.070 --> 00:09:50.520
work and the URL may change once made public
again.

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:53.580
You may also wish to save this collection.

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:59.680
In display setting, located in the blue tool
bar, click the down arrow to sort the collection

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:03.390
by date, author, or title.

00:10:03.390 --> 00:10:09.790
Additionally, items may be deleted by selecting
'all' or checking the box next to the citations,

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:13.570
clicking delete, and 'OK' to confirm.

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:19.500
Selected citations may be personally viewed
in the PubMed browser by clicking 'view'.

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:28.620
Finally, manage all collections from here
or from the My NCBI homepage by click Manage

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:30.270
collections.

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:35.190
Merge and delete are only available for custom
collections.

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:42.170
Meaning that Favorites, My Bibliography and
Other Citations cannot be merged or deleted.

00:10:42.170 --> 00:10:47.600
Also you are able to check the date last modified
by hovering over the text.

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:53.370
This concludes the brief tutorial on how to
create an automated search, create a collection

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:56.360
and activate a public URL.

00:10:56.360 --> 00:11:00.720
If there are any remaining questions, please
feel free to ask them at this time.

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:02.709
And once again thank you for joining us.

00:11:02.709 --> 00:11:08.180
[Peter Cooper speaking] Okay thank you Sherri,
there was one question in the Chat Box, I

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:13.410
did not answer, is it not possible to export
a collection to Endnote?

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:18.350
[Sherri Bailey] You cannot do this in your
personalized, customized collection, however

00:11:18.350 --> 00:11:25.230
you can do this either in My Bibliography,
or Other citations.

00:11:25.230 --> 00:11:30.590
There is a link after the questions, which
will give you a step-by-step method on how

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:35.810
to export from those collections, meaning
My Bibliography, or Other citations.

00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:41.209
[Peter Cooper] Another question, is there
a way to automatically save Collections as

00:11:41.209 --> 00:11:42.209
PDF's?

00:11:42.209 --> 00:11:44.730
[Sherri Bailey] Not at this time.

00:11:44.730 --> 00:11:49.180
That is a great suggestion we will pass on.

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:51.560
[Peter Cooper] Okay.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:54.810
Thank you I don't see any other questions
in the question pod.

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:59.220
Sherri is showing the last slide here, additional
documents you may find helpful.

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:03.519
There is a two minute PubMed Search Tutorial
available.

00:12:03.519 --> 00:12:09.060
And there is a YouTube video on using My Bibliography
and Other Citations.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:20.070
Just to remind you to keep up on NCBI see
the Insights blog, at ncbiinsights.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov.

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:27.529
And we do have a YouTube channel; ncbinlm
is the channel name.

00:12:27.529 --> 00:12:35.540
For any questions about NCBI resources, please
write to info@ncbi.nlm.nih.gov.

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:43.450
If you have specific questions about the webinars,
write to webinars, that's webinars@ncbi.nlm.nih.gov.

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:45.930
Thanks everyone for coming.

